{"case_id":"T8022","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API protocol","configuration","input semantics"],"confidence":96,"affected_functions":["xmlNewInputFromUrl","xmlNewInputFromMemory","xmlNewInputFromString","xmlNewInputFromFd","xmlNewInputFromIO","xmlInputSetEncodingHandler"],"reason":"S1 exposes a family of parser-input constructors in the public header include/libxml/parser.h, but H0 does not directly fuzz their distinct contracts. In particular, it does not generate callback behavior for xmlNewInputFromIO, file-descriptor and ownership states for xmlNewInputFromFd, flag combinations for xmlNewInputFromUrl and xmlNewInputFromMemory, null/size/termination edge cases, output-pointer error handling, or encoding-handler transitions. H0's xmlFuzzResourceLoader only constructs a fixed static, zero-terminated memory input, while genSeed.c is corpus-generation code rather than a fuzz entry point for these APIs.","evidence":["include/libxml/parser.h newly declares xmlNewInputFromUrl, xmlNewInputFromMemory, xmlNewInputFromString, xmlNewInputFromFd, xmlNewInputFromIO, and xmlInputSetEncodingHandler as public APIs.","xmlNewInputFromUrl has an int error-code plus xmlParserInputPtr *out protocol and accepts XML_INPUT_UNZIP and XML_INPUT_NETWORK flags; H0 has no fuzzed direct invocation covering out == NULL, filename == NULL, loader errors, or flag combinations.","xmlNewInputFromMemory accepts caller-controlled mem, size, XML_INPUT_BUF_STATIC, and XML_INPUT_BUF_ZERO_TERMINATED semantics, but xmlFuzzResourceLoader always uses the fixed combination XML_INPUT_BUF_STATIC | XML_INPUT_BUF_ZERO_TERMINATED.","xmlNewInputFromIO installs attacker-influenced ioRead, optional ioClose, and ioCtxt callbacks, including negative xmlParserErrors returns and close-on-allocation-failure behavior; H0 defines no such callback-state protocol.","xmlNewInputFromFd consumes an fd and documents that it is closed after parsing; H0 does not exercise descriptor validity, read failures, or ownership/closure behavior.","xmlInputSetEncodingHandler is declared alongside the new public input API, but H0 never applies it to independently constructed inputs."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated input-API fuzz target that selects among all public constructors, fuzzes URLs, buffers, sizes, termination/static flags, descriptors, callback read/error/close sequences, and encoding handlers, then consumes and frees each resulting xmlParserInputPtr while checking return/out-pointer and ownership invariants."}
